# RFC 8985 TLP (Tail Loss Probe): when there's un-ACKed data and no ACK
# movement, the stack sends a probe at PTO = max(2*SRTT, 10ms), well before
# the RTO would fire (200 ms floor).
#
# Two segments are in flight: with a single one, RFC 8985 §7.2 adds the
# worst-case delayed-ACK time (200 ms) to the PTO, which the RTO then caps.
#
# Setup: handshake (SRTT ~5 ms), send two segments, then NEVER ACK them.
# After 50 ms the probe has fired: with no new data to send, it
# retransmits the highest-sequence segment.

--connect 10.0.0.1:49152 10.0.0.2:80
+0 > SEW 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460, wscale 5, sackOK, TS val * ecr 0>
+.005 < S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 32768 <mss 1460, wscale 0, sackOK, TS val 1 ecr *>
+0 > . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 32768 <TS val * ecr 1>

# Two MSS-payload-sized segments (effective MSS = 1448 after TS option).
--send 2896
+0 > P. 1:1449(1448) ack 1 win 32768 <TS val * ecr 1>
+0 > P. 1449:2897(1448) ack 1 win 32768 <TS val * ecr 1>

# No ACKs come back. PTO = max(2*5 ms, 10 ms) = 10 ms.
+.050 > P. 1449:2897(1448) ack 1 win 32768 <TS val * ecr 1>
